<title>USA: US banks free reserves $669 mln/day rvsd July 2 wk.</title>
<headline>US banks free reserves $669 mln/day rvsd July 2 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $669 million per day in the two weeks ended July 2, versus revised free reserves of $1.007 billion in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $300 million versus $205 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
